# Quorix Cursor Rules

Before coding, read `CLAUDE.md` and all six files in `docs/`:
- `docs/01_PRD.md`
- `docs/02_AppFlow.md`
- `docs/03_UI_Spec.md`
- `docs/04_TRD.md`
- `docs/05_Schema.md`
- `docs/06_Plan.md`

## Workflow
- Inspect current source and manifests before editing.
- Plan first; identify files and tests affected.
- Make small, reviewable changes on a feature branch.
- Preserve existing behavior and architecture unless an approved decision changes it.
- Update `docs/06_Plan.md` when implementation status changes.
- Do not claim tests/builds/deployments passed unless actually run.
- Do not merge to the default branch without explicit user approval.

## Product and UI
- Quorix is Android-first.
- Use the exact approved Quorix logo asset; do not approximate it.
- Follow the dark Liquid Glass specification. Real backdrop blur where supported, translucency, reflective edges and depth are required; gradients alone are not Liquid Glass.
- Chat Mode and Thinking selectors belong inside the composer.
- Wallpaper controls belong in Settings > Appearance.
- Provider catalog must remain extensible.
- BOSS must show actual routing/agent execution, never simulated activity.
- AI Review is limited to five rounds.
- Android Device Control is native-only and permission-gated.

## Technical and security
- Verify framework versions from repository manifests.
- Verify provider API details from official documentation.
- Distinguish permanent free tiers, limited free tiers, trial credits and paid plans.
- Keep API keys and service-role credentials server-side.
- Never commit secrets or log credentials.
- Enforce authentication, workspace ownership and RLS.
- Require explicit confirmation for destructive device operations.
- Do not invent capabilities or mark untested integrations as working.

## Final response
Summarize changed files, tests actually run, remaining work and plan updates.
